    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493313408/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """London, Monday, Apr. 8, 1907
The operation — at 2 — proved very serious. It took 1 3/4 hours. Fortunately I stayed in, and was there for the doctor to consult as to whether he should do the “radical”. He said there was still a “sporting chance” for her hearing without it, but it would probably mean having to do it in the end. Of course I said to give her the chance.
But it is too awful.
Bernhard down to Assisi and then across to Perugia. He says Lady Sassoon gets nicer the more you are with her."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 120 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1907> .

